SUMMARY:UCL East Welcome Crafternoon
LOCATION:TBD
DESCRIPTION:Join Us for a Crafternoon with Sapphire\nTake a break\, get cre
 ative and make something meaningful at this special Crafternoon at UCL Eas
 t.\nDuring the session\, you’ll create positive affirmation cards for yo
 ung people and friendship cards for refugees and asylum seekers supported 
 by Sapphire.\nThese handmade cards will provide encouragement\, positivity
  and a sense of connection to people who may be experiencing feelings of i
 solation or facing challenges in their lives.\nYou don't need to be 'good'
  at art or have experience in making cards\, there will be enough material
 s and people there to help\, you just need a willingness to make something
  that could brighten someone's day!\nNo artistic experience is needed. All
  materials and guidance will be provided\, so just bring your creativity a
 nd a willingness to make something that could brighten someone’s day.\n
 🎨 What You’ll Be Creating\nYou’ll have the opportunity to create tw
 o types of handmade cards:\n🌟\nPositive affirmation cards\nencouraging 
 messages and artwork designed to inspire and uplift young people.\n💌\nF
 riendship cards\n– thoughtful messages and creative designs for refugees
  and asylum seekers\, helping to create a sense of connection and belongin
 g.\nYou can use your own ideas\, artwork and messages to make each card pe
 rsonal and meaningful.\n💚 About Sapphire\nSapphire is a charity that wo
 rks to support people in the community\, including young people\, refugees
  and asylum seekers\, with a focus on improving wellbeing\, reducing isola
 tion and helping people feel supported and connected.\nTheir work includes
  providing opportunities for people to access support\, build relationship
 s and take part in activities that promote wellbeing and community connect
 ion.\nDuring the Crafternoon\, members of the Sapphire team will introduce
  their organisation\, explain how the cards you create will support their 
 beneficiaries and share more about the work they do.\nThey’ll also be av
 ailable throughout the session to chat with students and answer ques…\n\
 nOrganised by UCL Student Social Impact.
URL:https://studentsunionucl.org/whats-on/volunteering/ucl-east-welcome-cra
 fternoon?v=95403
END:VEVENT
