SUMMARY:Welcome Crafternoon
LOCATION:Haldane Room\, Wilkins Building
DESCRIPTION:Join Us for a Welcome Crafternoon\nJoin us for a relaxed and cr
 eative Crafternoon during Welcome and the Volunteering Fair!\nIn this sess
 ion\, you’ll create handmade A5 cards featuring artwork\, creative desig
 ns and positive messages. The cards will be shared with young refugees and
  asylum seekers supported by Hope for the Young\, helping to create moment
 s of connection\, encouragement and positivity.\nNo artistic experience is
  needed. Whether you enjoy drawing\, writing\, designing or simply want to
  try something creative\, all materials and guidance will be provided.\n
 🎨 What You’ll Be Creating\nYou’ll have the opportunity to create ha
 ndmade A5 cards using a range of art materials.\nYour cards could include:
 \n🎨 Colourful artwork and illustrations\n💌 Positive and encouraging 
 messages\n🌟 Creative designs and decorations\n✍️ Short notes to bri
 ghten someone's day\nEach card will be given to a young person supported b
 y Hope for the Young\, giving your creativity a meaningful purpose beyond 
 the session.\n💚 About Hope for the Young\nHope for the Young\nis a char
 ity that supports young refugees and asylum seekers in the UK to overcome 
 barriers to education and wellbeing.\nSince 2008\, they have worked alongs
 ide young people to help them settle into their communities\, access educa
 tion and achieve their goals. Their work includes one-to-one mentoring\, f
 inancial support and advocacy\, providing tailored support based on each y
 oung person's needs and aspirations.\nDuring the Crafternoon\, a represent
 ative from Hope for the Young will introduce the organisation\, talk about
  the young people they support and explain how the cards you create will b
 e used.\n👥 What to Expect\n🎨\nGet Creative:\nCreate your own handmad
 e A5 cards using a range of materials.\n🤝\nMeet Other Students:\nWork a
 longside fellow students in a relaxed and welcoming environment.\n💚\nMa
 ke an Impact:\nCreate something that will be shared with young refugees an
 d asylum seekers supported by Hope for the Young.\n💡\nLearn More:\nHear
  directly from…\n\nOrganised by UCL Student Social Impact.
URL:https://studentsunionucl.org/whats-on/volunteering/welcome-crafternoon?
 v=95161
